{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "36ae9ce0-fe19-4a06-8608-f69691158b4b",
    "name": "Trustap API v1 - Guest User to Claim Flow (corrected hosts)",
    "description": "Sandbox walkthrough: create guest seller + buyer, create a P2P transaction between them, pay the deposit via Trustap's hosted checkout, accept the deposit, confirm handover, then claim the transaction for the seller's full Trustap account.\n\nFull sequence: 0 sanity check -> 1 create guest seller -> 2 create guest buyer -> 3 quote fee -> 4 create transaction (also builds {{pay_deposit_link}} in the console - open it in a browser and pay as the guest buyer) -> 5 accept deposit as guest seller -> 6 confirm handover as guest seller -> 7 claim for seller with the full account.\n\nHost correction (2026-07-22): `api-sandbox.trustap.com` (used elsewhere in the plugin) does NOT resolve - verified via DNS lookup and curl. The real Trustap API v1 hosts, confirmed against Trustap's own OpenAPI doc example and against the working host found during the 2026-07-18 debugging session in trustap-claim-seller-notes.md, are:\n- Staging/sandbox API: https://dev.stage.trustap.com\n- Live/production API: https://dev.trustap.com\n- Staging/sandbox hosted checkout (pay_deposit etc.): https://actions.stage.trustap.com/\n- Live/production hosted checkout: https://actions.trustap.com/\n\nSee trustap-guest-claim-implementation-plan.md for the related plugin bug (admin/class-t4e-pg-trustap-admin.php:205 still points at the dead api-sandbox host).\n\nStep 5 (accept_deposit_with_guest_seller) will 403 with code deposit_not_paid until the buyer actually completes payment at {{pay_deposit_link}} - this is a real browser/manual step, there's no pure-API way to submit card details for the deposit.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "18841506"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Sanity check (host + auth reachable)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK - host resolves and api_key is accepted', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "if (pm.response.code === 401) console.warn('401: api_key is wrong or blank - set the collection variable api_key before continuing.');"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/p2p/charge?currency=eur&price=1234",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "p2p",
            "charge"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "currency",
              "value": "eur"
            },
            {
              "key": "price",
              "value": "1234"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Run this first. If this fails to connect at all, base_url is wrong. If it 401s, api_key is wrong. If it 200s, you're good to proceed."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Create guest seller",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "const json = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('guest_seller_id', json.id);",
              "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "pm.test('has id', () => pm.expect(json.id).to.be.a('string'));"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {},
            "requests": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"\",\n  \"first_name\": \"Test\",\n  \"last_name\": \"Seller\",\n  \"country_code\": \"IE\",\n  \"tos_acceptance\": {\n    \"ip\": \"127.0.0.1\",\n    \"unix_timestamp\": {{$timestamp}}\n  }\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/guest_users",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "guest_users"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Creates a Trustap guest user to act as the seller. Response `id` is saved into {{guest_seller_id}} by the Tests script."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Create guest buyer",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "const json = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('guest_buyer_id', json.id);",
              "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "pm.test('has id', () => pm.expect(json.id).to.be.a('string'));"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {},
            "requests": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"rajufresh00@gmail.com\",\n  \"first_name\": \"Test\",\n  \"last_name\": \"Buyer\",\n  \"country_code\": \"IE\",\n  \"tos_acceptance\": {\n    \"ip\": \"127.0.0.1\",\n    \"unix_timestamp\": {{$timestamp}}\n  }\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/guest_users",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "guest_users"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Creates a Trustap guest user to act as the buyer. Response `id` is saved into {{guest_buyer_id}} by the Tests script."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Quote fee (charge)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const json = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('charge_amount', json.charge);",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('charge_calculator_version', json.charge_calculator_version);",
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/p2p/charge?currency=eur&price=1234",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "p2p",
            "charge"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "currency",
              "value": "eur"
            },
            {
              "key": "price",
              "value": "1234"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Returns the Trustap fee for a 1234 (smallest-unit) EUR item. `charge` and `charge_calculator_version` are saved for use in the transaction body."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Create guest-to-guest transaction",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Guards against the 'malformed_json: invalid character ,' error -",
              "// that happens when charge_amount/charge_calculator_version are empty",
              "// because request 3 (Quote fee) hasn't been run yet in this session.",
              "const chargeAmount = pm.collectionVariables.get('charge_amount');",
              "const chargeVersion = pm.collectionVariables.get('charge_calculator_version');",
              "const guestSeller = pm.collectionVariables.get('guest_seller_id');",
              "const guestBuyer = pm.collectionVariables.get('guest_buyer_id');",
              "",
              "const missing = [];",
              "if (!chargeAmount) missing.push('charge_amount');",
              "if (!chargeVersion) missing.push('charge_calculator_version');",
              "if (!guestSeller) missing.push('guest_seller_id');",
              "if (!guestBuyer) missing.push('guest_buyer_id');",
              "",
              "if (missing.length) {",
              "  throw new Error('Missing collection variable(s): ' + missing.join(', ') + '. Run requests 1, 2 and 3 first (or Run the whole collection top-to-bottom) before this request.');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('transaction_id', jsonData.id);",
              "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "pm.test('seller_is_guest is true', () => pm.expect(jsonData.seller_is_guest).to.eql(true));",
              "",
              "// Mimics PHP's http_build_query($state_parts, '', ':') + base64_encode()",
              "// from includes/gateways/class-override-gateway-trustap.php:173-201",
              "function phpUrlEncode(v) {",
              "  return encodeURIComponent(v).replace(/%20/g, '+');",
              "}",
              "",
              "const stateParts = {",
              "  token: (Math.random().toString(36) + Math.random().toString(36)).slice(2, 34),",
              "  order_id: pm.collectionVariables.get('test_order_id'),",
              "  name: pm.collectionVariables.get('test_buyer_name'),",
              "  line1: pm.collectionVariables.get('test_buyer_line1'),",
              "  city: pm.collectionVariables.get('test_buyer_city'),",
              "  state: pm.collectionVariables.get('test_buyer_state'),",
              "  postcode: pm.collectionVariables.get('test_buyer_postcode'),",
              "  country: pm.collectionVariables.get('test_buyer_country'),",
              "  tx_type: 'p2p'",
              "};",
              "",
              "const stateString = Object.entries(stateParts)",
              "  .map(([k, v]) => `${k}=${phpUrlEncode(v || '')}`)",
              "  .join(':');",
              "",
              "const stateBase64 = btoa(stateString);",
              "",
              "const payDepositUrl = pm.collectionVariables.get('actions_base_url')",
              "  + 'f2f/transactions/' + jsonData.id",
              "  + '/pay_deposit?redirect_uri=' + pm.collectionVariables.get('redirect_uri')",
              "  + '&state=' + stateBase64;",
              "",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('pay_deposit_link', payDepositUrl);",
              "console.log('Open this in a browser to pay the deposit as the guest buyer:');",
              "console.log(payDepositUrl);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"buyer_id\": \"{{guest_buyer_id}}\",\n  \"seller_id\": \"{{guest_seller_id}}\",\n  \"creator_role\": \"seller\",\n  \"currency\": \"eur\",\n  \"description\": \"Postman test item\",\n  \"deposit_price\": 1234,\n  \"deposit_charge\": {{charge_amount}},\n  \"charge_calculator_version\": {{charge_calculator_version}},\n  \"skip_remainder\": true\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/p2p/me/transactions/create_with_guest_user",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "p2p",
            "me",
            "transactions",
            "create_with_guest_user"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Creates a P2P transaction with both buyer and seller as guest users. Response `id` is saved into {{transaction_id}}. Tests script also builds {{pay_deposit_link}} - open the console after running this request to get the link, since the deposit must be paid via Trustap's hosted checkout before handover can be confirmed."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Accept deposit (guest seller)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK or already-accepted 403', () => {",
              "  pm.expect([200, 403]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
              "});",
              "if (pm.response.code === 403) {",
              "  const json = pm.response.json();",
              "  if (json.code === 'deposit_not_paid') {",
              "    console.warn('deposit_not_paid: open {{pay_deposit_link}} in a browser and complete payment as the guest buyer first, then re-run this request.');",
              "  } else if (json.code === 'deposit_already_accepted') {",
              "    console.log('Deposit was already accepted - safe to continue to the next request.');",
              "  } else {",
              "    console.warn('403: ' + json.code);",
              "  }",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Trustap-User",
            "value": "{{guest_seller_id}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/p2p/transactions/{{transaction_id}}/accept_deposit_with_guest_seller",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "p2p",
            "transactions",
            "{{transaction_id}}",
            "accept_deposit_with_guest_seller"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Guest seller accepts the buyer's paid deposit. No body. Requires the buyer to have already paid via {{pay_deposit_link}} (from request 4's console output) - otherwise returns 403 deposit_not_paid. Must succeed before handover can be confirmed."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Confirm handover (guest seller)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK or already-confirmed 400', () => {",
              "  pm.expect([200, 400]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Trustap-User",
            "value": "{{guest_seller_id}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/p2p/transactions/{{transaction_id}}/confirm_handover_with_guest_user",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "p2p",
            "transactions",
            "{{transaction_id}}",
            "confirm_handover_with_guest_user"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Guest seller confirms handover. A 400 with code seller_handover_already_confirmed is fine if this is re-run. Requires request 5 (accept deposit) to have succeeded first."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "7. Claim transaction for seller (full account)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  const json = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.test('seller_id now equals full account id', () => pm.expect(json.seller_id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('seller_full_user_id')));",
              "  pm.test('seller_is_guest is false', () => pm.expect(json.seller_is_guest).to.eql(false));",
              "}",
              "if (pm.response.code === 401) {",
              "  console.warn('401: seller full account has likely not completed OAuth Connect with this client in this environment yet - see trustap-claim-seller-notes.md');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Trustap-User",
            "value": "{{seller_full_user_id}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/p2p/transactions/{{transaction_id}}/claim_for_seller",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "p2p",
            "transactions",
            "{{transaction_id}}",
            "claim_for_seller"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Seller claims the transaction with their full Trustap account. Requires the full account to have completed OAuth Connect with this API key's client at least once in this environment - otherwise expect 401 unauthorized (see trustap-claim-seller-notes.md, 2026-07-18 debugging session)."
      },
      "response": []
    }
  ],
  "auth": {
    "type": "basic",
    "basic": [
